4:43'),(22611,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',845,NULL,'{\"text\": \"iv)???????????????? The base- is a firmly ossified structure that covers and protect the brain stem 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0, 0.5, 1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:43'),(22612,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',846,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Key features of the fetal skull are bones, sutures and fontanelles, which are membranous space. 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0, 0.5, 1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:43'),(22613,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',847,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Anatomical features are:   Bones- 2 frontal, 2parietal 2temporal and one occiput bones. 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0, 0.5, 1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:43'),(22614,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',848,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Sutures ?are fibrous joints that separates the bones. They are sagittal, coronal, lambdoid and frontal sutures. 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0, 0.5, 1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:44'),(22615,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',849,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Fontanelles ?are soft sports where two  or more sutures meets. There are two:  i) anterior fontanelles or bregma, is diamond in shape, situated at the junction of the sagittal, coronal and frontal sutures. It closes at 18 months. 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0, 0.5, 1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:44'),(22616,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',850,NULL,'{\"text\": \"ii)Posterior fontanelle (Lambda) is triangular in shape located at the junction of the sagittal and lambdoidel sutures. It closes earlier, at 6 months. 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0, 0.5, 1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:44'),(22617,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',851,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Importance of the fetal skull ? takes part during labor 1/2Mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:34:44'),(22618,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',852,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Student introduces self and task required   1/2marks\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22619,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',853,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Picks the model of the pelvis and fetus and places on the right occipito - posterior position 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22620,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',854,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Lie ? longitudinal, presentation ? cephalic, position ? ROPP  attitude ? deflexed, engaging diameter ? occipito posterior 11.5cm,  1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22621,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',855,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Engagement and descent ? the fetal head enters the pelvis in an oblique diameter instead of the transverse  1/2marks\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22622,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',856,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Flexion ? the fetus flexes so as to navigate the birth canal with the smallest diameter 1/2marks\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22623,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',857,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Internal rotation ?  With good flexion and uterine contractions, descent, the right occiput touches the pelvis floor muscles rotates 1/8th or 135 ? 155 degree forward to reach the symphysis pubis. (OA position)  1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22624,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',858,NULL,'{\"text\": \"If this long rotation fails, it results to persistent occipito posterior and baby is birth face to pubes 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22625,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',859,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Crowning / extension ? if long rotation occurs to AO position, the head extends the  pubic arch Crowning takes place  1 mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22626,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',860,NULL,'{\"text\": \"If POPP, the root of the nose engages under the symphysis pubis and the head flexes rather than extends to be delivered  1 mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22627,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',861,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Delivery of the head - External rotation/ restitution ? the head rotates back 45 degrees to align with the shoulders. 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22628,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',862,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Delivery of the shoulder/ body or expulsion ? The shoulders enters and touches the pelvic floor , rotates forward, the anterior shoulders passes under the symphysis pubis 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22629,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',863,NULL,'{\"text\": \"While the posterior shoulder is delivered and the body.1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:36:20'),(22630,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',864,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Student greets and introduces self and task 1/2\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22631,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',865,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Mention, in normal situation, assessment is quickly done in one minute and  five minutes, if baby is flabby 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22632,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',866,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Call for help 1/2mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22633,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',867,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Dry baby?s body with towel, wrapped warm under radiant heater 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22634,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',868,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Observe ? look for breat      -????????? Listing for air sound  -????????? Feel with back of palm for air 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22635,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',869,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Check heart rate using stethoscope, if below 60 bpm 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22636,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',870,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Position baby in neutral position by laying baby flat on surface and fold towel of 1 ? 2 thick under the shoulders to keep airway petend and see need for suctioning if there are secretions or meconeum 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22637,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',871,NULL,'{\"text\": \"If no response, go for CPR  1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22638,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',872,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Using ambu ? bag, wrapped with palm on both side of the chest with thumbs at 2 ? 3 cm below the lower stanum 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22639,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',873,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Give 3 rescue breaths, then observe, if no breathing, 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22640,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',874,NULL,'{\"text\": \"Give 3 chest compression to a breath and continue for 30 minutes 1mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.5,1\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22641,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',875,NULL,'{\"text\": \"At any stage the baby starts to breath connect to oxygen 1/2\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22642,0,'admin','system','INSERT','questions',876,NULL,'{\"text\": \"If after 30 ? 1hour there is no breathing, the Pediatricients takes over the management 1/2mark\", \"score_values\": \"0,0.25,0.5\"}','','','2026-03-02 18:37:32'),(22643,5,'examiner','examiner2','ASSESSMENT_SUBMITTED','answers',6407,NULL,'{\"exam_id\": 64, \"student_id\": 557, \"question_id\": 852, \"score\": 0.50}','','','2026-03-02 18:38:06'),(22644,5,'examiner','examiner2','ASSESSMENT_SUBMITTED','answers',6408,NULL,'{\"exam_id\": 64,