bour ','0,0.25,0.5'),(823,59,'Korcher\'sforcep- Methods of sterilization: Disinfect sterilize by HLD with chlorine solution of autoclaving ','0,0.25,0.5'),(824,59,'VOLSELLUM','0,0.25,0.5'),(825,59,'VOLSELLUM- Use: used to hold the uterus in procedures such as MVA, IUCD insertion ','0,0.25,0.5'),(826,59,'VOLSELLUM- Method of sterilization: HLD with 0.5% chlorine solution, boiling or auto cleaving ','0,0.25,0.5'),(827,59,'Handles instruments properly      ','0,0.25,0.5'),(828,59,'Misoprostol: ¼ Group- prostaglandin/utero tonic ','0,0.25,0.5'),(829,59,'M.O.A: Acts by stimulating uterine contraction ','0,0.125,0.25'),(830,59,'Dosage: 200mcg- 600mcg ','0,0.125,0.25'),(831,59,'R.O.A: Orally, rectally, sublingually ','0,0.125,0.25'),(832,59,'Indication: prevention and treatment of PPH','0,0.25,0.5'),(833,59,'Side effect: severe uterine pain, nausea vomiting, shivering, dizziness, excessive contraction ','0,0.25,0.5'),(834,59,'Group: Broad spectrum antibiotic ','0,0.125,0.25'),(835,59,'M.O.A -Acts by interfering with protein synthesis in bacterial cell wall ','0,0.25,0.5'),(836,59,'Indication UTI, Respiratory tract infection skin and soft tissue infection ','0,0.25,0.5'),(837,59,'R.O.A:  IM, IV Orally ','0,0.125,0.25'),(838,59,'Side effect: Nausea, vomiting ','0,0.125,0.25'),(839,65,'Student introduces self/task      1/2mark','0,0.25,0.5'),(840,65,'Pick the fetal skull model, introduce it as a model  1/2mark','0,0.25,0.5'),(841,65,'Defines the fetal skull as a flexible structure that undergoes molding in order to passed the maternal pelvis during birth. 1/2marks','0,0.25,0.5'),(842,65,'Comprises of the vault, face and base.: Region of the fetal skull are 4.:  i)The vault or caldarium- is the top part and most significant in child bearing. 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(843,65,'ii)The vertex- is at the area between the fontanelles 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(844,65,'iii) face- starts from the orbit/ridge to the chin 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(845,65,'iv)The base- is a firmly ossified structure that covers and protect the brain stem 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(846,65,'Key features of the fetal skull are bones, sutures and fontanelles, which are membranous space. 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(847,65,'Anatomical features are:   Bones- 2 frontal, 2parietal 2temporal and one occiput bones. 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(848,65,'Sutures ?are fibrous joints that separates the bones. They are sagittal, coronal, lambdoid and frontal sutures. 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(849,65,'Fontanelles are soft sports where two  or more sutures meets. There are two:  i) anterior fontanelles or bregma, is diamond in shape, situated at the junction of the sagittal, coronal and frontal sutures. It closes at 18 months. 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(850,65,'ii)Posterior fontanelle (Lambda) is triangular in shape located at the junction of the sagittal and lambdoidel sutures. It closes earlier, at 6 months. 1mark','0, 0.5, 1'),(851,65,'Importance of the fetal skull ? takes part during labor 1/2Mark','0,0.25,0.5'),(852,64,'Student introduces self and task required   1/2marks','0,0.25,0.5'),(853,64,'Picks the model of the pelvis and fetus and places on the right occipito - posterior position 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(854,64,'Lie  longitudinal, presentation  cephalic, position  ROPP  attitude deflexed, engaging diameter  occipito posterior 11.5cm,  1mark','0,0.5,1'),(855,64,'Engagement and descent the fetal head enters the pelvis in an oblique diameter instead of the transverse  1/2marks','0,0.25,0.5'),(856,64,'Flexion the fetus flexes so as to navigate the birth canal with the smallest diameter 1/2marks','0,0.25,0.5'),(857,64,'Internal rotation With good flexion and uterine contractions, descent, the right occiput touches the pelvis floor muscles rotates 1/8th or 135 ? 155 degree forward to reach the symphysis pubis. (OA position)  1mark','0,0.5,1'),(858,64,'If this long rotation fails, it results to persistent occipito posterior and baby is birth face to pubes 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(859,64,'Crowning / extension if long rotation occurs to AO position, the head extends the pubic arch Crowning takes place 1 mark','0,0.5,1'),(860,64,'If POPP, the root of the nose engages under the symphysis pubis and the head flexes rather than extends to be delivered  1 mark','0,0.5,1'),(861,64,'Delivery of the head - External rotation/ restitution ? the head rotates back 45 degrees to align with the shoulders. 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(862,64,'Delivery of the shoulder/ body or expulsion The shoulders enters and touches the pelvic floor , rotates forward, the anterior shoulders passes under the symphysis pubis 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(863,64,'While the posterior shoulder is delivered and the body.1mark','0,0.5,1'),(864,63,'Student greets and introduces self and task 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(865,63,'Mention, in normal situation, assessment is quickly done in one minute and  five minutes, if baby is flabby 1mark','0,0.25,0.5'),(866,63,'Call for help 1/2mark','0,0.5,1'),(867,63,'Dry babys body with towel, wrapped warm under radiant heater 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(868,63,'Observe ? look for breat      - Listing for air sound  - Feel with back of palm for air 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(869,63,'Check heart rate using stethoscope, if below 60 bpm 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(870,63,'Position baby in neutral position by laying baby flat on surface and fold towel of 1 ? 2 thick under the shoulders to keep airway petend and see need for suctioning if there are secretions or meconeum 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(871,63,'If no response, go for CPR  1mark','0,0.5,1'),(872,63,'Using ambu bag, wrapped with palm on both side of the chest with thumbs at 2 ? 3 cm below the lower stanum 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(873,63,'Give 3 rescue breaths, then observe, if no breathing, 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(874,63,'Give 3 chest compression to a breath and continue for 30 minutes 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(875,63,'At any stage the baby starts to breath connect to oxygen 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(876,63,'If after 30 1hour there is no breathing, the Pediatricients takes over the management 1/2mark','0,0.25,0.5'),(877,67,'APPEARANCE  1Mark','0,0.5,1'),(878,67,'COMPOSURE  1mark','0,0.5,1'),(879,67,'GREET PATIENT, INTRODUCE YOURSELF AND OBTAIN CONSENT 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(880,67,' Set tray, wheel to BED SIDE 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(881,67,'START WITH PATIENT?S TEMPERATURE,  PULSE AND BLOOD PRESSURE, TAKING NOTE OF ALL THE VITAL INDICES THAT MUST BE NOTED LIKE PULSE RYTHYM, VOLUME, NOTE ALSO THE DYSTOLIC READING VERY WELL. 1mark ','0,0.5,1'),(882,67,'REASSURE and GIVE PATIENT A CHANCE TO ASK QUESTIONS AND EXPRESS HIS/HER FEARS. 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(883,67,'IF THERE IS ANY DEVIATION FROM THE NORMAL RANGES, RECORD WITH A RED BIRO FOR ADEQUATE NOTICE AND ATTENTION. 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(884,67,'Make patient comfortable 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(885,67,'UNMASK AND DISCARD HAND GOVES, perform hand hygiene 1mark','0,0.5,1'),(886,67,'DOCUMENT PROCEDURE ON THE APPROPRIATE CHART.1mark','0,0.5,1'),(887,66,'ASSEMBLY THE INSTRUMENT 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(888,66,'CLARIFY THE ORDER 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(889,66,'INTRODUCE SELF AND PROCEDURE 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(890,66,'MAINTAIN PRIVACY 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(891,66,'WASH YOUR HANDS 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(892,66,'WEAR YOUR GLOVE 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(893,66,'Position the patient to expose the area and relieve pressure on it (e.g., side-lying). 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(894,66,'Removal of Old Dressing 1','0,0.5,1'),(895,66,'Gently remove the old dressing (using adhesive remover if necessary). Observe for drainage, odor, and color. 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(896,66,'Skin Inspection 1','0,0.5,1'),(897,66,'Assess the wound for staging (size, depth, exudate, slough, granulation). Note the condition of the surrounding skin (peri wound). 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(898,66,'Cleanse the ulcer using 0.9% Normal Saline. Use gentle, direct irrigation or moist gauze. Do not scrub. 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(899,66,'Apply a barrier cream to surrounding skin. Reposition the patient, ensuring the wound is not under direct pressure. 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(900,66,'Ensure the patient is comfortable. 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(901,66,'Turn patient every 2hours 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(902,66,'Wash your hand and remove glove 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(903,66,'Tidy your environment 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(904,66,'Make Patient comfortable 1/2','0,0.25,0.5'),(905,68,'Prepare Equipment:?Assemble linen (2 sheets, blanket, bedspread, pillowcase, mackintosh/drawsheet) on a clean trolley/chair in order of use. 1','0,0.5,1'),(906,68,'Hand Hygiene & PPE:?Perform hand hygiene; put on gloves if handling soiled linen. 1','0,0.5,1'),(907,68,'Position Bed:?Raise bed to a comfortable working height (waist level) and lock wheels. 1','0,0.5,1'),(908,68,'Remove Soiled Linen:?Loosen old linen, remove, and roll inwards (soiled side inside). Place in hamper; do not shake or let it touch your uniform. 1','0,0.5,1'),(909,68,'Clean Mattress:?If necessary, wipe mattress with disinfectant an1d allow to dry. 1','0,0.5,1'),(910,68,'Draw Sheet:?Place in the middle of the bed (under patient\'s back/hips) and tuck on both sides. 1','0,0.5,1'),(911,68,'Apply Top Linen:?Spread top sheet blanket, and spread. Tuck at the foot of the bed and miter corners. 1','0,0.5,1'),(912,68,'Pillow & Finish:?Apply pillowcase. Place pillow with open end away from the door. 1','0,0.5,1'),(913,68,'Lower the bed and ock its wheels to ensure patient safety 1','0,0.5,1'),(914,68,'REMOVE GLOVES AND WASH HANDS  1','0,0.5,1'),(915,76,'Greets and introduces self to patient','0,0.125,0.25'),(916,76,'Explain the procedure to the patient and obtains consent','0,0.125,0.25'),(917,76,'Request for an assistant, provide privacy by screening the bed','0,0.25,0.5'),(918,76,'Performs hand hygiene and wear gloves(clean)','0,0.25,0.5'),(919,76,'Loosens edges of plaster of the old dressing, stabilizes the skin with one hand while pulling the plaster in the opposite direction','0,0.25,0.5'),(920,76,'Beginning at the edges of the dressing, lifts the dressing towards the center of the wound','0,0.25,0.5'),(921,76,'If the dressing sticks, moistens it with 0.9% normal saline before removing it','0,0.25,0.5'),(922,76,'Observe remove dressing for drainage especially noting amount ,colour and odour','0,0.25,0.5'),(923,76,'Dispose soiled dressing and gloves and performs hand  hygiene','0,0.25,0.5'),(924,76,'Open sterile dressing supplies and sterile gloves using sterile technique','0,0.25,0.5'),(925,76,'Applies sterile normal saline from bottle or prefilled syringe onto sterile gauze or cotton balls using asterile technique','0,0.25,0.5'),(926,76,'Dons sterile gloves without contaminating or recognizing contamination','0,0.25,0.5'),(927,76,'Use a sterile cotton ball or gauze to cleanse the  wound','0,0.25,0.5'),(928,76,'Picks a new sterile dressing and places over the center of wound','0,0.25,0.5'),(929,76,'Places a large sterile ABD dressing over the wound dressing','0,0.25,0.5'),(930,76,'Secures edges of dressing to skin with plaster','0,0.25,0.5'),(931,76,'Places date, time and initial on dressing','0,0.25,0.5'),(932,76,'Discards used equipment properly','0,0.25,0.5'),(933,76,'Remove gloves and performs hand hygiene','0,0.25,0.5'),(934,76,'Thanks the patient and remove the screen','0,0.25,0.5'),(935,76,'Document procedure','0,0.25,0.5'),(936,78,'Greets and introduces self to patient','0,0.125,0.25'),(937,78,'Explain the procedure to the patient and obtains consent','0,0.125,0.25'),(938,78,'Request for an assistant, provide privacy by screening the bed','0,0.25,0.5'),(939,78,'Performs hand hygiene and wear gloves(clean)','0,0.25,0.5'),(940,78,'Loosens edges of plaster of the old dressing, stabilizes the skin with one hand while pulling the plaster in the opposite direction','0,0.25,0.5'),(941,78,'Beginning at the edges of the dressing, lifts the dressing towards the center of the wound','0,0.25,0.5'),(942,78,'If the dressing sticks, moistens it with 0.9% normal saline before removing it','0,0.25,0.5'),(943,78,'Observe remove dressing for drainage especially noting amount ,colour and odour','0,0.25,0.5'),(944,78,'Dispose soiled dressing and gloves and performs hand 